**Related Spec**: specs/266-fix-controller-path-rewriting-of-project-commands/

# File: scripts/__tests__/plugin-controller-path.test.mjs
#
# Generated from: specs/311-materialize-packaged-controller-paths-across-hosts/requirements.md
Feature: Materialize packaged controller paths across hosts
  Packaged execute, verify, and delivery prompts previously kept contributor-host
  absolute controller paths. Foreign hosts failed with MODULE_NOT_FOUND before
  the nmg-sdlc controller started. This was fixed by storing canonical
  <plugin-root> tokens and materializing both those tokens and recognized
  foreign nmg-sdlc/scripts paths onto the active installed package root.

  # --- Bug Is Fixed ---

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Foreign POSIX execute controller resolves on the active host
    Given a packaged execute prompt contains "node "/Users/rnunley/.omp/plugins/node_modules/nmg-sdlc/scripts/sdlc-execute.mjs""
    And the active installed plugin ships "scripts/sdlc-execute.mjs"
    When controller paths are materialized for that installed package
    Then the invocation is node plus the JSON-quoted active-host controller path
    And the emitted text does not contain "/Users/rnunley/.omp/plugins/node_modules/nmg-sdlc"
    And controller resolution does not fail with MODULE_NOT_FOUND

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Canonical and foreign packaged controllers resolve on every host
    Given packaged execute, verify, deliver, interactive, or worker text contains "<plugin-root>/scripts/<name>.mjs" or a foreign absolute nmg-sdlc/scripts/<name>.mjs path
    And the named controller is shipped by the active package
    When the prompt is materialized on Windows, macOS, or Linux path semantics
    Then each invocation uses the corresponding controller beneath the active installed package root
    And existing arguments after the controller path are preserved

  # --- Related Behavior Still Works ---

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Packaged artifacts stay host-neutral
    Given packaged workflow and file-command artifacts are generated or validated
    When the repository public-surface contract checks run
    Then every plugin-owned controller invocation is stored as "<plugin-root>/scripts/<name>.mjs"
    And no absolute nmg-sdlc/scripts/<name>.mjs controller path is accepted under commands/ or workflows/
    And generated command artifacts remain byte-identical to renderAutomatedCommandMarkdown

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: Project-local commands remain unchanged
    Given runtime text contains "node scripts/check-gate.mjs"
    And runtime text also contains a project-owned absolute path that does not identify nmg-sdlc/scripts/<name>.mjs
    When controller paths are materialized
    Then both project-local commands remain byte-for-byte unchanged
    And they are not redirected into the nmg-sdlc package

  # --- Edge Case ---

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: Missing packaged controller still fails closed
    Given a plugin-owned controller reference names "missing.mjs"
    And the active package does not ship "scripts/missing.mjs"
    When strict packaged-prompt materialization runs
    Then materialization fails with reason code "controller_unresolved"
    And no consumer-cwd or project-local script fallback is used
